1. The run's abort signal reaches every Mistral request: the raw stream
   fetch and structuredOutput's chat.complete (ai-mistral 0.6.11 on
   upstream main has neither). Upstream PR to be opened; remove when released.
2. A non-OK response's error carries its HTTP status and parsed body, and the
   RUN_ERROR forwards them as rawEvent, as the SDK-based adapters do since
   TanStack/ai#985. The rethrow after RUN_ERROR is upstream's (tested) and
   stays. Upstream PR to be opened; remove when released.
3. A stream that ends without a finish_reason ends in a RUN_ERROR (code
   incomplete-stream) instead of finishing as stop, and a data line that is
   not JSON fails the run instead of being skipped with a warning. Upstream
   PR to be opened; remove when released.
4. The terminal event carries the choice's finish_reason as
   metadata.providerStopReason, so the service decides every finish reason (model_length and error included) from
   the SDK's union (apps/api/src/lib/chat/provider-stop-reasons.ts) instead
   of reading an unhandled one as "stop". Remove when upstream exposes the
   raw reason.


